00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:58.100
Now, for deploying
the Stackdriver agents

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:00.140
on the On-Prem cluster,
it's really simple.

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:02.300
You just follow a
set of instructions.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.240
And it's done.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:06.020
So out of the box, you
get rich observability

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:08.930
for your hybrid
multi-cluster environment.

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.270
Now notice also that
here in this scenario

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:15.590
we surface a lot of key
information for you,

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:19.390
including the number of
incidents, pods that are ready,

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:23.300
memory and CPU utilization
with respect to your resources

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.980
and the limits that
you have configured.

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.717
Notice as well that
you've actually--

00:20:27.717 --> 00:20:30.050
even though Kubernetes doesn't
have a hierarchy per se--

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:32.060
we're taking advantage
of Kubernetes' labels

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:34.970
to give you a pre-curated
