00:21:16.070 --> 00:21:18.300
And for each of these
Kubernetes objects,

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:19.680
you get very rich information.

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.460
So for instance, I
can go and inspect--

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.330
let's inspect a pod right now.

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:25.400
And I immediately
get several metrics.

00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:27.260
I know that my pod is
ready and is running.

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:29.739
If there's any incidents open,
I can see it right there.

00:21:29.739 --> 00:21:32.030
And then I start to get some
information on my metrics,

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:34.980
like CPU, memory, and so on.

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:35.930
All the way down--

00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:37.700
and notice that
in the same place

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:40.820
as we move beyond
network usage, you'll

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.890
find that we also include logs.

00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:44.390
So that goes back
again to this idea

00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:47.000
of true and rich
observability, trying

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:50.210
to increase the signals
that are available to you

00:21:50.210 --> 00:21:54.650
at the right context in the
right time and right Kubernetes

00:21:54.650 --> 00:21:55.740
component.

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:58.672
So it is easier for you to
speed your root cause analysis

00:21:58.672 --> 00:22:00.380
when you're trying to
resolve an incident

00:22:00.380 --> 00:22:01.796
or to find things
when you're just

00:22:01.796 --> 00:22:02.950
doing proactive monitoring.

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:04.700
So we see snippets of
logs are right here.

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:07.040
And I could even go
deep down into logging

00:22:07.040 --> 00:22:09.560
to get more details here.

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:12.350
Now this is very much the
self-contained Kubernetes

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:12.850
monitoring.

00:22:12.850 --> 00:22:15.224
But of course, you can use it
with all the other features

00:22:15.224 --> 00:22:16.405
that Stackdriver has.

00:22:16.405 --> 00:22:19.220
Jerzy mentioned before
that Stackdriver already

00:22:19.220 --> 00:22:20.810
has a Prometheus collector.

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:23.370
So if you have a Prometheus
instrumentation already,

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:25.100
you can just have
that with Stackdriver.

00:22:25.100 --> 00:22:27.780
All your metrics will be
ingested without a change.

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:30.896
And if you're not using any
