Kubernetes Engine

00:29:29.800 --> 00:29:33.250
cluster receiving more traffic.

00:29:33.250 --> 00:29:35.310
So this give you a
little bit more time.

00:29:35.310 --> 00:29:39.510
So in the real world it's
like draining the traffic--

00:29:39.510 --> 00:29:41.730
will take some time.

00:29:41.730 --> 00:29:42.230
OK.

00:29:42.230 --> 00:29:43.580
So let's refresh again.

00:29:54.520 --> 00:29:57.550
So let's [INAUDIBLE]
fresh one more time

00:29:57.550 --> 00:29:58.640
and see what it can goes.

00:30:01.580 --> 00:30:02.080
Yep.

00:30:02.080 --> 00:30:03.250
As you can see here--

00:30:03.250 --> 00:30:06.880
so our Kubernetes Engine cluster
has receiving more traffic.

00:30:06.880 --> 00:30:08.750
And it will keep going up.

00:30:08.750 --> 00:30:12.680
So I think in this moment as an
encore engineer, I'm fairly--

00:30:12.680 --> 00:30:15.100
I'm reasonably confident
that the issue has

00:30:15.100 --> 00:30:17.030
